{
	"id": "sveltekit-og",
	"name": "SvelteKit OG",
	"repo": "ethercorps/sveltekit-og",
	"url": "https://github.com/ethercorps/sveltekit-og",
	"summary": "A SvelteKit library that generates Open Graph images from an HTML/CSS string or a Svelte component without a headless browser, using Satori and resvg or the Takumi engine.",
	"description": "The first diagram shows the public API (the Satori, Takumi and client ImageResponse classes, their option types and the font helpers); the second shows the server rendering pipeline from HTML or component to VNode tree to SVG and PNG through satori, resvg and takumi-js.",
	"notes": "Intersection option types (ImageOptions & ResponseImageOptions, TakumiImageOptions & TakumiResponseOptions) are drawn as one interface generalizing the image half, with the response fields folded in; ClientImageResponseOptions is a TS union, drawn as an interface with dependencies to its two alternatives. TS unions were narrowed to the main type (element: string, output: Uint8Array, font bytes: ArrayBuffer); TakumiImageOptions.fonts also accepts TakumiFontDescriptor (not drawn). Left out to stay under 14: client engines and client createImage, the sveltekitOG Vite plugin, and the emoji, defaults and error-handler helpers.",
